# Build artefacts. The bridge is compiled on demand into the user's cache
# directory (see `Metastatic.Adapters.Gleam.Subprocess`), never into the
# package, so nothing here should be committed.
/target

# A nested target directory appears whenever cargo is run from inside
# `vendor/` (e.g. to check the vendored crates in isolation). It is ~700 MB
# and would push the Hex package past its 134 MB uncompressed limit, so it is
# ignored rather than merely untracked.
vendor/target

# `vendor/Cargo.lock` is written by running cargo inside `vendor/`. The
# bridge's own `Cargo.lock` already pins the vendored graph, so this one is a
# byproduct and would otherwise ship as a second, potentially stale lock file.
vendor/Cargo.lock
